      "correct": false,
      "hit_at_5": true,
      "citation_precision": 0.5,
      "mode": "hybrid",
      "answer": "They chose sinusoidal positional encodings because they hypothesized that the sinusoid formulation would make it easy for the model to learn relative\u2011position relationships \u2013 for any fixed offset\u202fk, the encoding at position\u202fpos\u202f+\u202fk can be expressed as a linear function of the encoding at\u202fpos\u202f[1]. Additionally, experiments showed that learned positional embeddings produced nearly identical results, confirming that the sinusoidal version was sufficient [2].",
      "route_got": "document_question",
